// COMPATIBILITY SHIM — not a module anyone should import today.
//
// The calendar lives in `calendar.mjs`; this file exists only so that a member
// carrying an OLD `core` pack keeps loading after the engine has moved on.
//
// WHY IT MUST EXIST. The engine lane and the pack lane deliver in separate PRs on
// separate cycles, and pack delivery is version-gated per pack — so every member
// passes through a window holding the NEW engine beside an OLD pack, and nothing
// can close that window. A pack file importing an engine module is therefore a
// stale caller of an instantly-current engine, the same asymmetry `updates/*`
// already carries ("empty an export, never remove it"). Renaming this module
// without leaving the shim broke exactly that way (#1004): the old
// `packs/core/task-declaration-shape.mjs` failed to load, a pack that fails to
// load fails the mount's self-test, and the converge then refuses to land AT ALL
// — so the member cannot even receive the pack version that would fix it.
//
// WHAT IS HERE. Only the symbols a fielded pack version actually imports, which
// is one: `FREQUENCIES`. Re-exported, never re-declared, so the shim cannot drift
// from the calendar it stands in for.
//
// WHEN IT GOES. When no member's stamped `packVersions.core` names a version whose
// `task-declaration-shape.mjs` still imports this path — read the field, do not
// guess a release. `engine-pack-lane-shims.test.mjs` pins the surface meanwhile.
export { FREQUENCIES } from './calendar.mjs';
EOF
cat > engine/scheduler/run.mjs <<'EOF'
// COMPATIBILITY SHIM — the slot scheduler is deleted (#974), and nothing here
// schedules anything.
//
// It exists for the same reason `slots.mjs` beside it does: the engine lane and
// the pack lane deliver separately, so a member holds the new engine beside an old
// pack for a while, and two fielded pack files import this path. Deleting it
// outright broke a member's converge (#1004) — see that file's header for the full
// asymmetry.
//
// WHAT IS HERE. Only the two symbols a fielded pack version imports, each pointing
// at the module that owns it now:
//
//   ensureLabels    packs/basics/tasks/task-janitor/worker.mjs   → github.mjs
//   parseOverrides  packs/sheepdog/tasks/fleet-digest/worker.mjs → the bag parser
//
// `parseOverrides` cannot re-export: its home is a PACK now (sheepdog's
// param-bag.mjs), and the engine may not import a pack. It is therefore the one
// duplicated body here — kept byte-identical in behavior and pinned against the
// pack's copy by the shim test, which is the drift guard this repo's rules ask for
// when a value must live in two places.
//
// WHEN IT GOES. When no member's stamped `packVersions` names a `basics` or
// `sheepdog` version whose worker still imports this path — read the field, do not
// guess a release.
export { ensureLabels } from './github.mjs';

// `A=1,B=2`, newline-separated, or bare `A` (⇒ `'true'`). Values stay STRINGS with
// no truthiness coercion. The shape a fielded fleet-digest worker expects.
export function parseOverrides(raw) {
  const out = {};
  for (const part of String(raw ?? '').split(/[,\n]/)) {
    const token = part.trim();
    if (!token) continue;
    const eq = token.indexOf('=');
    if (eq === -1) out[token] = 'true';
    else out[token.slice(0, eq).trim()] = token.slice(eq + 1).trim();
  }
  return out;
}
EOF
